    {
      "id": "mc-1Jgd",
      "step": 0,
      "order": 1,
      "family": "other",
      "title": "Landscape: tiny city-state on a coast",
      "text": [
        "Monaco is a European **microstate** on the French Riviera, a few kilometres west of the border with Italy."
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "images": [],
      "locations": [],
      "lookalikes": [
        "IT"
      ],
      "credit": {
        "source": "Plonk It",
        "url": "https://www.plonkit.net/monaco",
        "licence": "CC BY-NC-SA 4.0"
      },
      "summary": "A tiny coastal city-state a few kilometres from the Italian border. If you see a dense, glitzy city squeezed onto a Mediterranean hillside, think Monaco.",
      "differs": [
        {
          "country": "IT",
          "how": "Italy is far larger with plenty of rural areas"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mc-dU2m",
      "step": 0,
      "order": 2,
      "family": "architecture",
      "title": "Houses: dense luxury apartment blocks",
      "text": [
        "Monaco is a **rich** and **densely populated** city state, with a Mediterranean feel to it. The architecture is similar to cities in southern France and northern Italy, but more luxurious. You will see a lot of apartment buildings, neoclassical details, and pastel colours. There are essentially no rural areas."
      ],
